@aaronfranke @akien-mga Thanks for your reviews, all remarks should be addressed.
@aaronfranke For the `StringName` return for `get_name()`, if it's wanted, I can make another PR for that.

> For the 3D character movement script, I'm tempted to suggest that there should be mouse movement for rotation, but rotating up/down is best done with a separate node for the head, so maybe it's out-of-scope for a one-script template. Or maybe we should just have @onready var head: Node3D = $Head and require users to provide a child node called Head (we already require a CollisionShape3D child for a character anyway). Or maybe we do both and have a separate script for this.

I thought about this during the development of this PR, I think it is better to keep a template without the need of a node setup to keep the thing simple and avoid confusion.
